From: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: fix uninitialized scan req use in
 ieee80211_start_roc_work

Patch 350 moved the ieee80211_can_leave_ch() check to the top of
ieee80211_start_roc_work(), before the point where `req` is dereferenced
from local->scan_req, so the check reads an uninitialized pointer. The
pointer reaches ieee80211_is_radar_required(), which dereferences it
whenever a link has radar_required set — undefined behavior on any ROC
request while operating on a DFS channel. GCC compiles this silently;
clang rejects it with -Werror,-Wuninitialized (how it was found, 2026-07-12
system-clang build).

Hoist the wiphy_dereference() above the check and drop the now-dead later
assignment (nothing after it reads `req` since patch 350 removed the
ieee80211_is_radar_required() call from the queue-or-immediate test).

--- a/net/mac80211/offchannel.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/offchannel.c
@@ -610,6 +610,7 @@ static int ieee80211_start_roc_work(stru
 	if (!local->emulate_chanctx && !local->ops->remain_on_channel)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
+	req = wiphy_dereference(local->hw.wiphy, local->scan_req);
 	cfg80211_chandef_create(&chandef, channel, NL80211_CHAN_NO_HT);
 	radio_mask = ieee80211_chandef_radio_mask(local, &chandef);
 	if (!ieee80211_can_leave_ch(sdata, req, radio_mask) &&
@@ -650,8 +651,6 @@ static int ieee80211_start_roc_work(stru
 		roc->mgmt_tx_cookie = *cookie;
 	}
 
-	req = wiphy_dereference(local->hw.wiphy, local->scan_req);
-
 	/* if there's no need to queue, handle it immediately */
 	if (list_empty(&local->roc_list) && !local->scanning) {
 		/* if not HW assist, just queue & schedule work */
